{
  "about": "The Great Lakes rocky-shore recipe (Tier C, VerticalSlicePhasePlan.txt §10). One shared grammar: zone files in Tools/Biomes/zones/ say where it applies; Tools/EditorScripts/biome/plan.py turns both into placements; scatter.py writes them as NoCollision HISM into Lvl_PointeSombre_Biome. Every number here is a tuning value, not a geographic fact (the slope, height, and density starting points came from the Gemini shoreline brief and were then tuned against the captures). Metres unless a key says otherwise. The terrain's own surfaces (rock, shingle, turf, seabed by slope and height) do most of the work; these families only sit on it. Disabled families (litter, decals, trees, wet-band) are deliberately absent from v1 (VS-06 scope); add one as a new entry with enabled false first, never as a code path.",
